Flux_Attr_std|Std dev of flux attraction|probability
Flux_Repu_std|Std dev of flux repulsion|probability
.TE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "measurement \(em Phase 3.5: Observer Modules"
Four read-only measurement algorithms that extract physics from
existing simulation data.  All measurements are optional and
activated via CLI flags (\fB\-\-measure\-all\fR or per-module flags).
.TP
.B "M1 \(em Cover-Time Mass (Topological Inertia)"
Measures the dynamical mass of each Causal Prism via coupon-collector
cover time on the defect CSR.  A confined random walker must visit
\fBevery\fR belly node before exiting at the destination pole.  Cover
time scales as O(N\~log\~N) \(em heavier generations (larger bellies)
require more causal ticks for full internal phase coherence.  If the
walker reaches the destination before full coverage, it reflects back
to the origin (incomplete phase update).  The K\d2,N\u hitting-time
theorem proves that simple origin\(->\~destination traversal is O(1)
regardless of N; cover time is the correct dynamical mass observable.
.TP
.B "M2 \(em Half-Life Census"
Cross-ensemble stability statistics.  For each prism, records
generation, belly size, and net phase.  Computes occupancy fractions
p(gen\dk\u\~|\~N) per belly size and stability ratios
\(*t(gen2)/\(*t(gen1), \(*t(gen3)/\(*t(gen1).  At N=5000, M=8:
occupancy fractions 4%/79%/17% match the zero-parameter occupancy
model prediction (2%/85%/13%).
.TP
.B "M3 \(em Modulo Path Integral"
NTT-based interference fringes from walker phases.  Walkers carry a
modular phase g\uS\d\~mod\~p (default: g=3, p=65537) where S counts
cumulative moves.  Per-node phase accumulation via AtomicU64.
Post-processing computes intensity (squared centred phase), classifies
constructive/destructive nodes.  Requires N\~\(>=\~50k for spatial
resolution.
.TP
.B "M4 \(em Vacuum Polarization"
K\d3,3\u screening at Gen1 prism free ports.  For each Gen1 prism,
counts candidate nodes that could extend it to K\d3,3\u (connecting to
both poles AND \(>=\~3 intermediates).  Screening factor =
n\daccepted\u\~/\~n\dattempted\u.  At N=5000: zero screening (vacuum
too sparse for K\d3,3\u), which is the correct finite-size behaviour.
.PP
.B MeasurementResult
aggregate struct:
.B traversal
(Option<TraversalMassResult>),
.B half_life
(Option<HalfLifeResult>),
.B modulo
(Option<ModuloPathResult>),
.B vacuum_pol
(Option<VacuumPolResult>).
.PP
Output files (when enabled):
.B traversal_mass.csv
(cover-time mass ratios per generation),
.B half_life.csv
(occupancy fractions and stability ratios),
.B modulo_interference.csv
(per-node phase accumulation),
.B vacuum_polarization.csv
(per-prism screening factors).
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "memory \(em RAM-Aware Mode Selection"
Detects available system RAM, estimates memory requirements, and
recommends in-memory or streaming mode.
.TP
.BI "load_config(" dir ") \(-> Config"
Load configuration from a TOML file, or return defaults.  Searches for
.I causal_set.toml
in the given directory first, then falls back to the current working
directory.
.TP
.BI "ensure_config(" dir ")"
Write the default config file if it doesn't already exist.
.TP
.BI "recommend_mode(" n ", cfg) \(-> (ExecMode, available, estimated)"
Recommend an execution mode based on config + available RAM vs estimated
usage.  The estimate accounts for concurrent realisations.
.TP
.BI "prompt_mode(" recommended ", available, estimated, cfg) \(-> ExecMode"
Prompt the user to confirm or override the recommended execution mode.
.TP
.BI "estimate_memory_bytes(" n ") \(-> u64"
Heuristic peak memory estimate: N\~\(<=\~3k uses ~N\(S2\(mu24 bytes;
3k\~<\~N\~\(<=\~50k uses ~N\(mu2000; N\~>\~50k uses ~N\(mu500.
.TP
.BI "max_concurrent_runs(" n ") \(-> usize"
Default concurrency: 2 for N\~>\~10M, 4 otherwise.
Overridable via
.BR \-\-threads .
.TP
.BI "available_ram_bytes() \(-> u64"
Detect available system RAM in bytes via
.BR sysinfo .
.PP
.B ExecMode
enum:
.B InMemory
or
.BR Streaming .
.PP
.B Config
struct:
.B max_ram_bytes
(hard ceiling, 0 = auto),
.B safety_fraction
(0.0\(en1.0),
.B output_dir
(default directory).
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I N
Number of spacetime events (default: 5000).
.TP
.I M
Ensemble realisations (default: 10).
.TP
.I output_dir
Directory for results (default: current directory or
.I causal_set.toml
setting).
.TP
.B \-\-stream
Force streaming mode (low RAM, writes edges to disk).
.TP
.B \-\-inmemory
Force in-memory mode (fast, needs sufficient RAM).
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " u64
Base seed for deterministic runs.  Each realisation uses seed + i.
Default: system clock nanos (real entropy).  The chosen seed is printed
at startup so non-seeded runs can be reproduced.
.TP
.BI "\-\-threads " usize
Maximum parallel realisations.  Default: auto (2 for N > 10M in-memory,
4 otherwise; streaming capped at CPU count or 8).
.TP
.BI "\-\-epsilon " f64
Topological error tolerance \(*e for the Causal Resolution Theorem.
Default: 0.01.
.TP
.BI "\-\-tmax " usize
Maximum diffusion time.  Default: 15.
.TP
.BI "\-\-eigen\-cutoff " N
Eigendecomposition threshold.  Graphs with N \(<= cutoff use exact
eigendecomp; larger graphs use Monte Carlo walkers.  Default: 3000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-target\-error " f64
Relative standard error threshold for adaptive convergence.
Default: 0.05.  The ensemble loop stops early when the relative
standard error of mass_gen1 drops below this value.
.TP
.BI "\-\-max\-ensemble " usize
Maximum number of realisations (hard cap).  Default: 22.
.TP
.BI "\-\-min\-ensemble " usize
Minimum realisations before convergence checks begin.  Default: 3.
.TP
.BI "\-\-batch\-size " usize
Realisations per parallel batch.  Default: auto (same as
.BR \-\-threads ).
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume from a previously saved checkpoint.  Reads
.I checkpoint.bin
from the output directory.
.TP
.BI "\-\-export\-slice " PATH
Export a single realization's topology to a binary
.I .slice
file (bincode format) and exit.  Runs Phases 1\(en2 only (no spectral
walkers, no ensemble averaging).  The output contains 4D coordinates,
directed Hasse edges (past\~\(->\~future), and Causal Prism definitions.
Intended for feeding pre-computed topology data to external renderers
such as CausalAnim.
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-mass
Enable cover-time mass ratios (M1).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-halflife
Enable half-life census (M2).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-modulo
Enable modulo path integral (M3).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-vacuum
Enable vacuum polarization (M4).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-all
Enable all four measurement modules.
.TP
.BI "\-\-modulo\-prime " u64
Prime modulus for M3 (Fermat number).  Default: 65537 (F\d4\u).
.TP
.BI "\-\-modulo\-root " u64
Primitive root for M3.  Default: 3.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
