.SS "Occupancy Model (Analytical Mass Hierarchy)"
The mass hierarchy m\d1\u < m\d2\u < m\d3\u is a coupon-collector selection
effect on the belly size distribution f(N).  Each intermediate carries a
causal phase \(*f(w) = sign(out_deg \- in_deg) \(mo {\-1, 0, +1}.
Generation g(P) counts how many distinct phase signs appear among the N
intermediates.  Since P(g=1|N) ~ p\dmax\u\uN\d decays exponentially,
Gen1 prisms are biased toward small bellies (low mass), while Gen3
requires all three signs (large bellies, high mass).
.PP
The simulation reports the intermediate phase census:
(p\d+\u, p\d0\u, p\d\-\u) = (0.318, 0.018, 0.664).  Plugging these
into the occupancy formula reproduces the mass ratios with zero free
